  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I had an animator break because some node somewhere in some layer had a VRCAnimatorLayerControl referencing a layer by its index, and I had inserted a new layer before it.\nObviously in the ideal case I'd want this to use an ID, but I'm assuming there is a really good reason why it isn't.\nAs layers get reorganised over time, the name is probably a more stable choice for something to identify the layer.\nYou could argue that the name could be renamed as well, but consider this:\nCase 1, you find a node somewhere referencing layer \"3\", but you don't know what 3 used to be.\nCase 2, you find a node somewhere referencing layer \"mouth\", but you have a layer called \"face\" so _maybe_ it got renamed to be more general at some point.",
